The Kernel-Target Alignment (KTA) for PQK was $0.5524$, slightly higher than that of the Fidelity Kernel ($0.5375$), reflecting stronger geometric alignment with the ground truth phase labels.

\subsection{Noise Robustness and Variance Decay}
Table \ref{tab:noise_res} records kernel behavior under increasing depolarizing error $p$. While classification accuracy remains high under exact optimization, the off-diagonal variance of the Fidelity Kernel collapses rapidly from $0.1563$ to $0.0412$ (a $73.7\%$ drop). In contrast, PQK off-diagonal variance drops only marginally from $0.1606$ to $0.1497$ ($6.8\%$).

