\section{Conclusion}
We have presented an empirical evaluation of quantum kernel methods on the 1D Transverse Field Ising Model under realistic noise and sampling limits. Our experiments demonstrate that Projected Quantum Kernels offer both high sample efficiency and resilience against noise-induced variance decay compared to global fidelity kernels. Future investigations will extend this benchmark to 2D frustrated lattices and test implementation on physical superconducting quantum hardware.

